Bilkul 👍 Ye pura section HTTP/HTTPS + URL + Requests/Responses + Methods + Status Codes + Headers + Cookies ke baare mein hai. Isko cybersecurity/CTF perspective se simple Hinglish mein samjho.

🌐 1. HTTP kya hai?

HTTP = HyperText Transfer Protocol

Simple language mein:

HTTP web browser aur web server ke beech communication ke rules hain.

Jab tum browser mein website open karte ho:

Browser
   ↓ HTTP Request
Web Server
   ↓ HTTP Response
Browser


Example:

Browser → "Mujhe homepage chahiye"
Server  → "Ye raha homepage"


HTTP ke through HTML, images, videos, CSS, JavaScript etc. transfer ho sakte hain.

🔐 2. HTTPS kya hai?

HTTPS = HTTP Secure

HTTPS basically HTTP communication ko TLS encryption/security ke saath protect karta hai.

Simple:

HTTP
Browser ───────────── Server
       readable traffic

HTTPS
Browser ═════════════ Server
       encrypted traffic


HTTPS ka purpose:

🔒 Confidentiality

Traffic ko beech mein dekhna difficult hota hai because data encrypted hota hai.

✅ Server authentication

TLS certificates help karte hain verify karne mein ki connection expected server/domain se establish ho raha hai.

🛡️ Integrity

Data ko transit mein tamper kiya gaya hai ya nahi, uski protection milti hai.

🔗 3. URL kya hai?

URL = Uniform Resource Locator

URL basically browser ko batata hai:

Kis protocol se, kis server par, kis resource ko access karna hai.

Example:

http://user:password@tryhackme.com:80/view-room?id=1#task3


Isko pieces mein todte hain:

http://
   ↓
scheme

user:password@
   ↓
credentials

tryhackme.com
   ↓
host

:80
   ↓
port

/view-room
   ↓
path

?id=1
   ↓
query string

#task3
   ↓
fragment

4. URL ke parts 🧩
Scheme
http://
https://
ftp://


Batata hai kaunsa protocol/use scheme use karna hai.

User

Example:

user:password@


Historically URL mein credentials include kiye ja sakte hain.

Note: Real-world use mein credentials ko URL mein rakhna generally avoid kiya jata hai because URLs logs/history mein expose ho sakte hain.

Host
tryhackme.com


Ya IP address:

192.168.1.10


Ye batata hai kis server ko access karna hai.

Port
:80


Port batata hai kis network service ko connect karna hai.

Common:

HTTP  → 80
HTTPS → 443


Lekin technically services other ports par bhi run kar sakti hain.

Path
/view-room


Server par requested resource/location ko identify karta hai.

Query String
?id=1


Server ko additional information/parameters bhej sakta hai.

Example:

/blog?id=10


Meaning:

Blog resource se ID 10 wala content chahiye.

Multiple parameters:

/search?q=dns&page=2

Fragment
#task3


Ye page ke specific location/section ko refer karta hai.

Important point:

Fragment generally browser-side hota hai aur normally HTTP request mein server ko send nahi hota.

📩 5. HTTP Request

Browser server ko request bhejta hai.

Example:

GET / HTTP/1.1
Host: tryhackme.com
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 Firefox/87.0
Referer: https://tryhackme.com/



Breakdown:

GET
GET /


Browser bol raha hai:

"Mujhe / resource chahiye."

HTTP/1.1

HTTP protocol version.

Host
Host: tryhackme.com


Server ko batata hai kaunsi website/resource target hai.

Ek server multiple websites host kar sakta hai, isliye Host header important hai.

User-Agent
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 ...


Client/browser ke baare mein information.

Referer

Batata hai request kis previous page/context se aayi.

Blank line

Headers ke end ko indicate karti hai.

📤 6. HTTP Response

Server request ka answer deta hai:

HTTP/1.1 200 OK

Server: nginx/1.15.8
Date: ...
Content-Type: text/html
Content-Length: 98

<html>
...
</html>


First line:

HTTP/1.1 200 OK


Ismein:

HTTP/1.1 → protocol version
200      → status code
OK       → status message

📊 7. HTTP Status Codes

Ye bahut important hain.

Range	Meaning
100–199	Informational
200–299	Success
300–399	Redirection
400–499	Client error
500–599	Server error

Easy trick:

1xx → "Wait / information"
2xx → "Success ✅"
3xx → "Go somewhere else ↪️"
4xx → "Tumhari request mein problem ❌"
5xx → "Server ki problem 💥"

⭐ Important Status Codes
200 OK

Request successful.

200 = Everything good ✅

201 Created

New resource successfully create hua.

Example:

POST /users
→ 201 Created

301 Moved Permanently

Resource permanently doosri location par move ho gaya.

302 Found

Temporary redirect.

400 Bad Request

Request malformed/incorrect hai.

Example:

Missing parameter
Invalid syntax

401 Unauthorized

Authentication required/failed.

Example:

Login required


Yaad rakho:

401 → Authentication problem

403 Forbidden

Server ne request samajh li, but access deny kar diya.

403 → "I know what you want, but NO."

404 Not Found

Requested resource nahi mila.

404 → Page doesn't exist

405 Method Not Allowed

Resource exist karta hai, but HTTP method allowed nahi.

Example:

/create-account


expects:

POST


but tum:

GET


bhej rahe ho.

Result:

405 Method Not Allowed

500 Internal Server Error

Server ke andar unexpected problem.

503 Service Unavailable

Server temporarily request handle nahi kar pa raha.

Possible reasons:

Maintenance
Overload
Service unavailable
🛠️ 8. HTTP Methods

HTTP method server ko batata hai:

"Main tumse kya action karwana chahta hoon?"

GET

Data retrieve karna.

GET /products


"Products do."

POST

Data submit/create karna.

POST /users


"Ye new user create karo."

PUT

Existing resource ko update/replace karna.

PUT /users/10

DELETE

Resource delete karna.

DELETE /users/10

Shortcut:
GET    → Read
POST   → Create/Submit
PUT    → Update
DELETE → Delete

📋 9. HTTP Headers

Headers = extra information/metadata jo request/response ke saath bheji jaati hai.

Request Headers

Client → Server

Host
Host: example.com


Kaunsi website/resource target hai.

User-Agent
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0


Browser/client information.

Content-Length

Batata hai request body mein kitna data expected hai.

Mostly POST/PUT jaise requests mein useful.

Accept-Encoding

Client kaunsa compression support karta hai.

Example:

Accept-Encoding: gzip

Cookie

Client server ko previously stored cookie bhejta hai.

Cookie: session=abc123

Response Headers

Server → Client

Set-Cookie

Server browser ko cookie store karne ko bolta hai.

Set-Cookie: session=abc123

Cache-Control

Browser/proxy ko batata hai response ko cache kaise handle karna hai.

Content-Type

Extremely important.

Batata hai returned data kis type ka hai.

Examples:

text/html
text/css
application/javascript
image/png
application/pdf
video/mp4


Browser is information se decide karta hai data ko kaise process karna hai.

Content-Encoding

Response kis compression method se encoded/compressed hai.

🍪 10. Cookies

Cookie ko simple language mein:

Browser mein stored small piece of website-related data.

HTTP itself stateless hai.

Meaning:

Request 1 → Server
Request 2 → Server
Request 3 → Server


Server inherently automatically ye assume nahi karta ki teeno requests same user/session se hain.

Cookies is problem ko solve karne mein help karti hain.

🔑 Login Example

Suppose tum website par login karte ho.

Server:

Set-Cookie: session=abc123


Browser cookie store kar leta hai.

Next request:

Cookie: session=abc123


Server samajh sakta hai:

"Ye existing logged-in session hai."

🧠 Cookie ka important point

Cookie mein usually directly:

password=myPassword123


nahi hota.

Instead commonly ek session identifier/token hota hai.

Example:

session=8f92a7c1...


Server apni side par identify kar sakta hai ki ye token kis session/user se associated hai.

🔥 Cybersecurity mein Cookies kyun important hain?

Because authentication often session cookies ke through maintain hoti hai.

Agar kisi attacker ko valid session cookie mil jaye aur server usse valid maan le, toh session hijacking jaise attacks possible ho sakte hain.

Isliye cookies ke security attributes important hote hain, jaise:

Secure
HttpOnly
SameSite


Ye next-level web security topics mein bahut important hain.

